---
import Container from '../ui/Container.astro';
import SectionTitle from '../ui/SectionTitle.astro';
import { profile } from '../../data/profile';
---

<section class="py-24">
  <Container>
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] lg:items-start">
      <div
        class="flex h-20 w-20 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-border bg-panel font-display text-xl font-semibold text-text-secondary"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        MS
      </div>
      <div>
        <SectionTitle eyebrow="About" title="Solving business problems with platform engineering" />
        <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-lg text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            {profile.name} is a {profile.title.toLowerCase()} based in {profile.location}, with 20 years of
            experience spanning full-stack development, cloud infrastructure, and platform automation.
            The work has consistently centered on one question: how does a growing engineering
            organization keep shipping reliably as its systems get more complex?
          </p>
          <p>
            That question has shown up as a legacy-to-cloud-native migration for a 200+ microservices
            platform, as a device-management layer for 50,000+ IoT devices monitoring public
            infrastructure, and as the CI/CD and observability practices that let small teams operate
            systems at that scale without growing headcount linearly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</section>
